@@ -0,0 +1,78 @@
+# Append-only static Twee importer
+
+This is a **restricted static import profile**, not a general Twine interpreter.
+It accepts a local UTF-8 `.twee` file plus independently supplied rights metadata.
+It makes no network calls, never runs JavaScript and never silently discards a
+macro, hook, unsupported passage or broken link to fabricate a playable graph.
+
+## Supported profile
+
+Declare `import_profile: kiro-twee3-static-v1` in metadata. A single `StoryTitle`
+contains the title. Optional `StoryData` may contain standard layout metadata,
+a v4 uppercase IFID, source story-format identifiers and an explicit start name.
+Format identifiers are preserved in the source archive, not executed. Without an
+explicit start the start passage is `Start`. Conflicting starts are errors.
+
+Passage headers support names and optional position/size metadata. The only
+supported tag is `[ending]`. Narration is plain text. A passage's links must be a
+final block, one per line. Supported forms: `[[Target]]`, `[[Label|Target]]`,
+`[[Label->Target]]`, `[[Target<-Label]]`. Destination names are preserved as exact
+IDs, including Unicode. IDs are URL-encoded by the common renderer.
+
+Declare each ending with `[ending]` or metadata `ending_passages`. A passage with
+no links is NOT assumed to be an ending. Endings cannot have successors. At least
+two endings, all targets present, complete reachability and no cycles are required.
